1
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:23,867
Drifting on the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:23,917 --> 00:00:26,840
aiming for that day,

3
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:31,481
if I kick a pebble,

4
00:00:31,531 --> 00:00:34,000
even my shoes went flying,

5
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:42,300
onto the head of the
carpenter who was choking,

6
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:48,440
and they laughed that I'm still just a kid.

7
00:00:48,440 --> 00:00:55,280
Even if I stir up some energy somewhere,
Katsushika is no use.

8
00:00:55,280 --> 00:01:02,560
Not even a yawn changes,
the streets strangely gentle.

9
00:01:03,780 --> 00:01:16,800
From the pointed hat and the water bottle,
the natural bow and the sunset fall.

10
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:25,260
Tomorrow too,
it'll end just like this, won't it.

11
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:29,060
Katsushika, Shibamata, happiness again.

12
00:01:29,060 --> 00:01:31,760
I only realized it after losing it.

13
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:34,020
Because I'm such a fool.

14
00:02:01,980 --> 00:02:03,040
There you are.

15
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:06,120
Ryo, wake up, boss.

16
00:02:10,020 --> 00:02:12,240
Tch, what a pain.

17
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:16,200
Senpai, please wake up, senpai.

18
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:18,160
What is it?

19
00:02:18,840 --> 00:02:20,920
It's already past three o'clock.

20
00:02:22,220 --> 00:02:25,580
I was sleeping so peacefully,
let me sleep some more.

21
00:02:25,580 --> 00:02:28,540
We'll get scolded if we don't head back now.

22
00:02:28,540 --> 00:02:32,280
Besides, patrol cars have been
gathering here for a while now.

23
00:02:33,100 --> 00:02:34,680
Fine, I'm coming.

24
00:02:41,180 --> 00:02:41,900
Senpai

25
00:02:43,680 --> 00:02:46,920
Sorry, I forgot you were
the plumbing guy, Oira.

26
00:02:51,460 --> 00:02:53,180
That wake-up dive really worked

27
00:02:53,180 --> 00:02:54,540
That woke me right up.

28
00:02:54,540 --> 00:02:57,000
That's what you get for
sleeping somewhere like that.

29
00:02:59,060 --> 00:03:00,260
What's wrong?

30
00:03:00,260 --> 00:03:01,460
My wallet's gone.

31
00:03:01,940 --> 00:03:03,540
I dropped it at Kanomaka.

32
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:05,380
That's rotten luck.

33
00:03:06,440 --> 00:03:07,440
We're definitely finding it.

34
00:03:10,740 --> 00:03:13,720
You're still doing unbelievable things,
as always.

35
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:15,320
But...

36
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:18,920
I wonder which matters more,
my body or my money.

37
00:03:27,880 --> 00:03:30,840
Ugh, what a filthy river this is!

38
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:35,620
What happened? You're soaked!

39
00:03:38,320 --> 00:03:40,120
I fell into the river for a bit.

40
00:03:40,740 --> 00:03:44,500
Honestly, you dove in twice
because you dropped your wallet.

41
00:03:45,380 --> 00:03:46,940
Well, you'll catch a cold.

42
00:03:48,320 --> 00:03:50,800
I found it in the sludge
at the bottom of the river.

43
00:03:51,220 --> 00:03:53,120
It was pitch black, so it was hard to find.

44
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:55,860
Going in without even goggles, you really...

45
00:04:01,080 --> 00:04:02,440
There sure are a lot of people today.

46
00:04:03,020 --> 00:04:05,700
There were plenty of them around
the embankment earlier, too.

47
00:04:05,700 --> 00:04:08,000
Senpai, did you do something again?

48
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:09,220
I don't know anything about it.

49
00:04:09,220 --> 00:04:10,460
I absolutely don't know.

50
00:04:10,460 --> 00:04:13,040
This is a serious situation!

51
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:14,740
What's wrong, Chief?

52
00:04:14,740 --> 00:04:16,160
It's a spill accident.

53
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:17,880
What's that supposed to mean?

54
00:04:17,880 --> 00:04:19,920
A truck carrying hazardous materials...

55
00:04:31,500 --> 00:04:34,880
The chemicals that had built up
spilled into the river in huge amounts.

56
00:04:35,480 --> 00:04:38,840
The whole area is contaminated,
and it's causing a huge commotion.

57
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:42,400
That bridge is near the floodgate?

58
00:04:43,260 --> 00:04:44,540
That's right. You know it?

59
00:04:44,780 --> 00:04:47,420
Ryotsu was swimming there just now, Senpai.

60
00:04:47,420 --> 00:04:48,460
What?

61
00:04:49,320 --> 00:04:52,580
Ryotsu,
why were you swimming in a place like that?

62
00:04:52,580 --> 00:04:57,680
At first I fell in, and then I dove in to
look for the wallet that fell into the river.

63
00:04:58,200 --> 00:05:02,380
Now that you mention it, I thought it
was strange that fish were floating around.

64
00:05:02,840 --> 00:05:03,800
How awful.

65
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:07,160
After that, I dove for about
an hour looking for my wallet.

66
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:08,920
What a greedy guy.

67
00:05:08,920 --> 00:05:11,060
So how are you feeling?

68
00:05:11,060 --> 00:05:13,420
I'm fine.

69
00:05:14,620 --> 00:05:16,640
Now that you say that, I actually feel...

70
00:05:18,460 --> 00:05:19,100
Oh no, this is bad!

71
00:05:19,240 --> 00:05:20,400
We need to call an ambulance!

72
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:21,460
Senpai!

73
00:05:28,440 --> 00:05:30,820
Well, I don't think there's anything wrong,
Ryo-san.

74
00:05:30,940 --> 00:05:31,540
Really?

75
00:05:31,820 --> 00:05:35,300
Yes. No diarrhea, no poisoning,
and no skin irritation at all.

76
00:05:35,740 --> 00:05:39,700
We're still waiting on the test results from earlier,
but I'm sure you'll be fine.

77
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:41,280
Well, that's a relief.

78
00:05:42,460 --> 00:05:43,520
Doctor, excuse me.

79
00:05:47,040 --> 00:05:47,260
I see.

80
00:05:47,940 --> 00:05:48,660
What did you say!

81
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:49,920
Got it.

82
00:05:50,440 --> 00:05:52,460
Ryotsu-san, please wait just like that.

83
00:05:56,880 --> 00:05:58,580
A new type of antibody?

84
00:05:59,820 --> 00:06:03,040
Yes, we found it while testing Mr. Ryotsu.

85
00:06:03,600 --> 00:06:05,567
As you all know,

86
00:06:05,617 --> 00:06:11,120
humans have a biological defense system
that works to keep the body healthy.

87
00:06:11,540 --> 00:06:14,760
Thanks to it,
we don't get sick from minor things.

88
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:19,540
Even when foreign matter invades,
these antibodies protect the body.

89
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:23,340
Human antibodies are
generally all the same shape.

90
00:06:23,340 --> 00:06:26,460
But Ryotsu's antibodies

91
00:06:29,220 --> 00:06:31,220
are shaped like this.

92
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:35,000
Unbelievable.

93
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:37,420
They look just like cartoon germs!

94
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:40,520
Don't be surprised yet.

95
00:06:40,520 --> 00:06:43,100
Since the structure is different,
when we examined it in detail,

96
00:06:45,280 --> 00:06:46,540
Take a look at this footage.

97
00:06:47,600 --> 00:06:51,500
The moment a virus gets near this antibody,
it's about to explode!

98
00:06:51,500 --> 00:06:53,840
In no time at all, it wipes out the virus.

99
00:06:53,840 --> 00:06:56,680
What an incredible homeostatic function!

100
00:06:56,680 --> 00:06:58,080
It's so fast!

101
00:06:58,500 --> 00:06:59,460
It's terrifying.

102
00:06:59,820 --> 00:07:04,640
Normally, antibodies are produced to fight
viruses that enter the body through colds and such.

103
00:07:05,160 --> 00:07:07,600
During that time, the cold symptoms persist.

104
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:10,560
But in his case, there are none.

105
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:12,960
No virus stands a chance against it.

106
00:07:14,760 --> 00:07:18,280
We can make a super-versatile
vaccine that no virus can withstand!

107
00:07:18,280 --> 00:07:20,400
It's the strongest vaccine in history!

108
00:07:22,520 --> 00:07:26,120
Professor,
why were such special antibodies created?

109
00:07:27,920 --> 00:07:28,840
In my opinion,

110
00:07:28,890 --> 00:07:33,260
at first, ordinary antibodies
were released from the lymphocytes,

111
00:07:33,260 --> 00:07:37,340
but then he was contaminated and the
environment became the worst possible,

112
00:07:37,340 --> 00:07:41,380
so the lymphocytes released antibodies
hardened to endure that filth,

113
00:07:41,380 --> 00:07:43,680
and when he was again soiled and battered,

114
00:07:43,680 --> 00:07:46,000
even stronger antibodies were born,

115
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:48,200
and to the point where
he could never recover,

116
00:07:48,200 --> 00:07:50,560
even when he was reduced to a hellish state,

117
00:07:51,040 --> 00:07:54,340
he rose again and again like a phoenix,

118
00:07:54,340 --> 00:07:58,300
and that's how the strongest
antibodies in history were made.

119
00:08:00,220 --> 00:08:02,980
They're antibodies that crawled up
from the hell of a terrible environment.

120
00:08:02,980 --> 00:08:04,880
Pretty tough, isn't he?

121
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:09,740
According to his data up to now,

122
00:08:11,400 --> 00:08:12,820
he has never once been sick,

123
00:08:13,280 --> 00:08:14,340
yet

124
00:08:14,340 --> 00:08:17,280
for over thirty years,
not a single illness at all.

125
00:08:19,780 --> 00:08:20,140
Amazing.

126
00:08:20,660 --> 00:08:21,560
Too amazing.

127
00:08:23,200 --> 00:08:25,580
It's all thanks to these antibodies.

128
00:08:26,140 --> 00:08:28,460
If we can make a cold remedy with these,

129
00:08:28,460 --> 00:08:29,580
it'll be worthy of a Nobel Prize.

130
00:08:30,100 --> 00:08:32,200
We can't let him leave this hospital.

131
00:08:32,200 --> 00:08:34,660
Let's all win the Nobel Prize together!

132
00:08:41,960 --> 00:08:45,400
I don't know if you'll like the meal,
but please, help yourself.

133
00:08:45,400 --> 00:08:47,420
You've suddenly gotten awfully nice.

134
00:08:47,420 --> 00:08:50,540
You're hiding something, aren't you?

135
00:08:50,540 --> 00:08:51,940
No, not at all.

136
00:08:54,580 --> 00:08:55,480
Hey, come on.

137
00:08:55,480 --> 00:08:57,280
Sorry.

138
00:08:57,280 --> 00:09:01,240
Since Mr. Ryotsu's antibodies are extremely rare,
we need to run further tests.

139
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:03,620
I knew it. That's what this was about.

140
00:09:04,040 --> 00:09:05,780
Don't go poking into things
that don't concern you.

141
00:09:07,900 --> 00:09:09,700
If there's nothing wrong with me,
I've got no reason to stay.

142
00:09:09,700 --> 00:09:10,380
I'm going home.

143
00:09:11,380 --> 00:09:11,980
You can't go!

144
00:09:11,980 --> 00:09:12,760
See ya!

145
00:09:15,220 --> 00:09:16,820
You're going to cooperate with us!

146
00:09:16,940 --> 00:09:18,660
Cooperate for the sake of humanity!

147
00:09:18,700 --> 00:09:19,720
Calm down!

148
00:09:20,020 --> 00:09:22,900
Who'd cooperate with that crap? Spill it!

149
00:09:24,400 --> 00:09:24,940
Professor!

150
00:09:25,240 --> 00:09:27,240
You said it's a miracle cold cure,

151
00:09:27,380 --> 00:09:31,020
that it's a groundbreaking medicine
unlike any cold remedy before, right?

152
00:09:31,380 --> 00:09:33,400
If that's true, it's Nobel Prize material!

153
00:09:34,180 --> 00:09:37,940
It's true.
We've finally discovered that vaccine.

154
00:09:38,420 --> 00:09:39,240
We've named it,

155
00:09:39,840 --> 00:09:42,720
Ryo-chi GPX

156
00:09:56,540 --> 00:09:59,360
The media has been causing
a huge commotion every day

157
00:09:59,360 --> 00:10:03,900
Yeah, absolutely. What started as a
fluke turned into an incredible discovery.

158
00:10:04,440 --> 00:10:07,160
Honestly,
what kind of body does he even have?

159
00:10:08,100 --> 00:10:12,980
Come to think of it, he once said he used to eat mud
and leaves without a second thought when he was a kid.

160
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:16,240
He also said he once ate dog
poop just to test his courage.

161
00:10:17,340 --> 00:10:20,540
I heard that when he was in elementary school,
he walked all the way to Osaka.

162
00:10:20,540 --> 00:10:22,100
All the way to Osaka?

163
00:10:22,760 --> 00:10:25,980
He said he used to run around
about 30 kilometers a day, so...

164
00:10:26,480 --> 00:10:29,660
It's like he's challenging his
physical limits every single day.

165
00:10:30,220 --> 00:10:32,660
And even as an adult,
his drive hasn't changed at all.

166
00:10:33,140 --> 00:10:35,100
So that's how he developed these antibodies.

167
00:10:40,600 --> 00:10:43,620
Well, from today this will be your room.

168
00:10:44,560 --> 00:10:47,240
This is the most luxurious
suite in the hotel.

169
00:10:51,100 --> 00:10:53,380
What a magnificent view,
what a magnificent view!

170
00:10:53,840 --> 00:10:57,200
Wow, a suite at a first-class
hotel really is different.

171
00:10:57,200 --> 00:10:59,600
But why are you doing all this?

172
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:01,980
You're a celebrity now, after all.

173
00:11:02,420 --> 00:11:06,920
The media is swarming the hospital,
and it's inconveniencing the other patients.

174
00:11:08,160 --> 00:11:11,180
Speaking of which,
I hear things are going crazy out there.

175
00:11:11,180 --> 00:11:14,020
Please, whatever you do,
don't leave this room.

176
00:11:14,380 --> 00:11:18,560
We can't have you coming into contact
with anyone except people we approve.

177
00:11:18,560 --> 00:11:22,160
No wonder they're being so careful,
with a Nobel Prize riding on this.

178
00:11:22,160 --> 00:11:25,700
Don't be ridiculous.
This research is going to save humanity.

179
00:11:25,700 --> 00:11:29,300
Fine, fine.
But TV and a VCR alone are boring.

180
00:11:29,300 --> 00:11:32,960
Get me a Jan-Taku video game console, and
while you're at it, a pachinko machine too.

181
00:11:33,740 --> 00:11:36,400
If you don't like it,
maybe I'll just go to another hospital.

182
00:11:37,160 --> 00:11:40,100
W-wait, that's a problem.
You, get those ready right away.

183
00:11:40,280 --> 00:11:41,040
Yes!

184
00:11:43,420 --> 00:11:44,500
And also...

185
00:11:45,820 --> 00:11:46,900
There's more?

186
00:11:47,160 --> 00:11:51,700
Assign the most beautiful nurse in
this hospital to take care of me.

187
00:11:51,760 --> 00:11:52,400
That's too much...

188
00:11:52,400 --> 00:11:54,100
If you don't like it, I'll go.

189
00:11:54,160 --> 00:11:54,980
F-fine, I understand.

190
00:11:57,220 --> 00:11:59,760
Well, this is getting interesting.

191
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:20,160
Yes.

192
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:26,040
Is it good?

193
00:12:26,940 --> 00:12:27,980
It's the best.

194
00:12:27,980 --> 00:12:30,160
On top of being served by two beauties,

195
00:12:30,160 --> 00:12:31,820
the food's a delight too.

196
00:12:32,280 --> 00:12:34,680
But I'm already tired of this hotel's suite.

197
00:12:34,680 --> 00:12:37,960
From tomorrow,
put me in a deluxe suite at another hotel.

198
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:40,120
A room that costs around five
hundred thousand a night, got it?

199
00:12:41,040 --> 00:12:42,500
Yes, I'll inform the professor.

200
00:12:44,620 --> 00:12:47,120
Mr. Ryotsu,
there's a visitor from Katsushika Station.

201
00:12:47,620 --> 00:12:48,260
Figures.

202
00:12:49,360 --> 00:12:51,200
Ryotsu, are you doing well?

203
00:12:51,200 --> 00:12:54,200
Ryotsu, thanks to you,
our station has become famous.

204
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:56,960
When you address me, you should say
"Sensei."

205
00:12:57,300 --> 00:12:57,620
What?

206
00:12:58,340 --> 00:13:01,340
Fine, if you don't want to.
Little baby won't cooperate, will he?

207
00:13:02,300 --> 00:13:03,820
Sensei, please calm down.

208
00:13:04,960 --> 00:13:08,200
How could you do this?
The future of humanity is at stake!

209
00:13:13,120 --> 00:13:19,000
Ryotsu-sensei, we've come today to inform you
that headquarters has promoted you four ranks.

210
00:13:20,220 --> 00:13:28,060
A four-rank promotion, so from patrol officer you'd go to sergeant,
inspector, chief inspector, and superintendent, right?

211
00:13:28,060 --> 00:13:30,780
It's the biggest
promotion in police history!

212
00:13:30,780 --> 00:13:33,240
What was the chief's rank again?

213
00:13:35,680 --> 00:13:39,540
Then little old me would like the rank above that,
superintendent-general.

214
00:13:39,540 --> 00:13:41,500
Y-you dare get cocky!

215
00:13:41,500 --> 00:13:43,480
Oharu-kun, c-chief.

216
00:13:45,740 --> 00:13:46,384
But...

217
00:13:46,434 --> 00:13:50,600
If we provoke him carelessly, our heads could roll.
We have to endure this.

218
00:13:50,980 --> 00:13:51,380
Yes.

219
00:13:51,980 --> 00:13:55,720
Understood, Doctor.
I'll go to headquarters and look into it.

220
00:13:56,160 --> 00:14:00,146
Of course. Thanks to me, colds will
be wiped out across the entire planet.

221
00:14:00,196 --> 00:14:02,060
So I'm the one saving the Earth.

222
00:14:03,060 --> 00:14:03,860
Well, then, that's all.

223
00:14:04,220 --> 00:14:04,840
Wait a moment.

224
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:06,980
Is there anything else?

225
00:14:06,980 --> 00:14:11,540
When you leave, you have to properly say,
"Excuse us, Doctor."

226
00:14:11,540 --> 00:14:13,620
I'm going to get upset, you know.

227
00:14:14,500 --> 00:14:17,460
If you're going to make that face,
fine, I won't cooperate then.

228
00:14:17,460 --> 00:14:21,240
I'll say it: "Excuse us, Doctor."

229
00:14:22,100 --> 00:14:23,440
This feels great.

230
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:27,060
That Ryotsu is getting
too big for his boots.

231
00:14:27,060 --> 00:14:30,600
Well, there's no helping it.
He's humanity's savior now, after all.

232
00:14:30,600 --> 00:14:34,560
It's the end of the world when a
guy like that is considered a savior.

233
00:14:35,980 --> 00:14:36,880
That tickles.

234
00:14:41,760 --> 00:14:42,640
Die.

235
00:14:43,480 --> 00:14:43,920
This is

236
00:14:44,860 --> 00:14:45,580
Professor.

237
00:14:45,580 --> 00:14:49,820
Incredible.

238
00:14:54,620 --> 00:14:55,500
Is that really true?

239
00:14:55,500 --> 00:14:58,640
Does it even fight off cancer cells?

240
00:14:58,640 --> 00:14:59,960
Not only cancer,

241
00:14:59,960 --> 00:15:01,640
but athlete's foot, night crying,

242
00:15:01,640 --> 00:15:02,940
even kan-no-mushi,

243
00:15:02,940 --> 00:15:04,800
it's effective against everything.

244
00:15:05,680 --> 00:15:11,700
GPX is truly invincible. This is the greatest
and last great discovery of the century.

245
00:15:22,260 --> 00:15:29,620
Must be nice living in a room this luxurious!
And the hospital's covering all your meals too

246
00:15:29,620 --> 00:15:32,160
Hey, pour some wine for Volvo.

247
00:15:41,040 --> 00:15:44,060
Looks like that was a
bit too much for Volvo.

248
00:15:45,640 --> 00:15:47,460
Ron, it's the third dragon set.

249
00:15:48,440 --> 00:15:50,080
A million again?!

250
00:15:50,080 --> 00:15:52,580
As the dealer, that's 48,000 points.

251
00:15:52,580 --> 00:15:55,740
Here, the rest is a loan.

252
00:15:55,740 --> 00:15:57,880
Maria is winning everything.

253
00:15:57,880 --> 00:16:00,300
I can feel some incredible intensity.

254
00:16:00,300 --> 00:16:01,900
Of course.

255
00:16:02,400 --> 00:16:03,910
Even though I'm right here,

256
00:16:03,960 --> 00:16:07,320
why is a sexy woman like
this taking care of Ryo-san?

257
00:16:07,960 --> 00:16:12,180
W-well, it's because humanity's
dreams and future depend on him.

258
00:16:13,920 --> 00:16:16,920
And what does that have to
do with this sexy uniform?!

259
00:16:17,260 --> 00:16:18,580
It's suffocating!

260
00:16:29,060 --> 00:16:30,780
Hey, what's wrong? Pull yourself together!

261
00:16:30,880 --> 00:16:32,860
We just put him to sleep for a little while.

262
00:16:32,860 --> 00:16:33,700
Who are you?

263
00:16:34,760 --> 00:16:36,160
We're not suspicious characters.

264
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:38,860
At the request of the Russian government,

265
00:16:38,860 --> 00:16:41,700
we've come to pick up Mr. Riatsuon.

266
00:16:42,440 --> 00:16:44,240
The Russian government has asked me

267
00:16:44,240 --> 00:16:48,360
to develop the Ryocchi GPX in Russia,
if at all possible.

268
00:16:48,880 --> 00:16:51,040
We've brought a check for one billion yen.

269
00:16:52,020 --> 00:16:53,440
One billion yen!?

270
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:56,480
If you come to Russia with me,

271
00:16:56,480 --> 00:16:58,560
Britain will pay two billion yen.

272
00:17:00,800 --> 00:17:02,340
And it's in cash!

273
00:17:05,760 --> 00:17:07,540
Maybe I'll go to Britain, then.

274
00:17:08,400 --> 00:17:09,200
Wait a minute!

275
00:17:10,120 --> 00:17:12,660
France has prepared five billion yen.

276
00:17:12,660 --> 00:17:14,060
Please come to France!

277
00:17:14,440 --> 00:17:17,840
We'll offer the same terms.

278
00:17:17,840 --> 00:17:22,040
And we'll add a villa on a 500-tsubo plot!

279
00:17:23,180 --> 00:17:24,440
Then France will...

280
00:17:26,220 --> 00:17:27,800
offer a 1,000-tsubo villa and...

281
00:17:59,880 --> 00:18:00,500
It's settled.

282
00:18:00,880 --> 00:18:03,320
The helicopter is on standby, so

283
00:18:06,280 --> 00:18:07,480
That's the one.

284
00:18:07,480 --> 00:18:08,820
Coming!

285
00:18:10,760 --> 00:18:14,340
W-who would do something like this?

286
00:18:16,600 --> 00:18:17,920
This music...

287
00:18:29,700 --> 00:18:31,820
I knew it was you, Colonel Bakuryu.

288
00:18:33,900 --> 00:18:36,140
Long time no see, Mr. Ryotsu.

289
00:18:36,140 --> 00:18:39,580
I've come to take you at the
request of the American government.

290
00:18:39,580 --> 00:18:41,060
Now, come with me.

291
00:18:42,220 --> 00:18:44,560
I'm the hottest commodity around,
with everyone fighting over me.

292
00:18:44,560 --> 00:18:46,800
We're offering five billion
yen and a beautiful woman!

293
00:18:51,840 --> 00:18:53,480
We'll take him by force.

294
00:18:56,840 --> 00:18:59,460
You idiot, there's a condition like that?

295
00:19:01,020 --> 00:19:02,260
Running away is pointless.

296
00:19:08,980 --> 00:19:11,260
I will never hand you over.

297
00:19:14,700 --> 00:19:16,520
The helicopter was shot
down by the U.S. military.

298
00:19:16,520 --> 00:19:18,760
Quickly, arrange another means of transport.

299
00:19:18,760 --> 00:19:19,920
It's useless.

300
00:19:19,920 --> 00:19:22,440
You shouldn't underestimate Colonel Bakuryu.

301
00:19:24,200 --> 00:19:24,980
Halt!

302
00:19:35,280 --> 00:19:36,460
This is too much.

303
00:19:36,460 --> 00:19:37,560
Didn't I tell you?

304
00:19:37,560 --> 00:19:39,420
Didn't I warn you not to
underestimate Colonel Bakuryu?

305
00:19:43,500 --> 00:19:44,820
Looks like we lost them.

306
00:19:44,820 --> 00:19:45,860
Keep going like this.

307
00:19:46,640 --> 00:19:47,500
Red light!

308
00:19:52,280 --> 00:19:52,840
Ugh, come on!

309
00:19:53,260 --> 00:19:55,020
Oh no! They've spotted us!

310
00:19:56,340 --> 00:19:58,682
At this point,
it's easier for me to escape alone.

311
00:19:58,732 --> 00:20:01,000
Let's meet in the lobby
of Paradise Hospital.

312
00:20:01,280 --> 00:20:01,940
Got it.

313
00:20:18,280 --> 00:20:19,440
Ryotsu, Kankichi isn't here!

314
00:20:20,440 --> 00:20:22,900
What? At the intersection just now!

315
00:20:27,480 --> 00:20:29,560
Damn! They've caught up already!

316
00:20:30,040 --> 00:20:30,980
Wanikanza!

317
00:20:31,360 --> 00:20:32,220
Whoa! Hey!

318
00:20:32,800 --> 00:20:34,280
Found you, Ryotsu!

319
00:20:34,480 --> 00:20:37,320
Give up quietly and come to America with me!

320
00:20:37,900 --> 00:20:38,620
No way!

321
00:20:48,480 --> 00:20:48,900
I'll get you for this!

322
00:20:51,780 --> 00:20:55,120
Trying to escape from me
is ten years too early!

323
00:21:00,740 --> 00:21:02,380
W-wait!

324
00:21:11,120 --> 00:21:13,400
Hey! Can you get up here?

325
00:21:13,620 --> 00:21:15,200
Let me in!

326
00:21:22,360 --> 00:21:23,620
No way!

327
00:21:26,680 --> 00:21:29,520
How did you get into the subway?!

328
00:21:30,820 --> 00:21:33,040
Don't go pulling some
subway manzai routine on me.

329
00:21:33,040 --> 00:21:36,200
Don't you know there's such a
thing as a vehicle loading entrance?

330
00:21:37,880 --> 00:21:38,660
Stop it!

331
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:43,660
Give up and come to America.

332
00:21:43,660 --> 00:21:46,480
Damn it... after all this...

333
00:21:48,840 --> 00:21:49,480
This is it!

334
00:21:54,500 --> 00:21:55,400
We're going to crash!

335
00:22:03,880 --> 00:22:04,780
We did it, we did it!

336
00:22:08,400 --> 00:22:09,380
Out of the way!

337
00:22:09,380 --> 00:22:11,100
With this,
we're off to France with beautiful women!

338
00:22:15,620 --> 00:22:19,260
I forgot we were in a tunnel.

339
00:22:29,280 --> 00:22:30,520
What's all that commotion?

340
00:22:30,520 --> 00:22:33,460
The reason we've gathered
you all here on short notice

341
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:36,620
is to deliver some sad news.

342
00:22:37,260 --> 00:22:38,620
Sad news?

343
00:22:38,860 --> 00:22:39,580
What?

344
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:44,680
It's been determined that the
Ryocchi GPX vaccine can't be used.

345
00:22:45,380 --> 00:22:47,240
What? That's

346
00:22:47,240 --> 00:22:49,640
It's simply too powerful.

347
00:22:50,320 --> 00:22:55,260
It's an antibody that can only
exist in a body as tough as Ryo-san's.

348
00:22:55,860 --> 00:22:58,220
Administering the vaccine to ordinary people

349
00:22:58,220 --> 00:23:01,260
is like making a child
chug a bottle of vodka.

350
00:23:01,700 --> 00:23:02,980
We focused only on the antibody

351
00:23:03,460 --> 00:23:06,000
and failed to account for
his off-the-charts body.

352
00:23:07,060 --> 00:23:09,700
So it's completely useless, then?

353
00:23:10,520 --> 00:23:11,600
That's right.

354
00:23:14,240 --> 00:23:14,560
No way...

355
00:23:14,560 --> 00:23:14,980
No way!

356
00:23:18,740 --> 00:23:20,160
I can't be bothered with this anymore.

357
00:23:25,760 --> 00:23:28,720
Hey, the five-rank demotion
is happening too, right?

358
00:23:29,500 --> 00:23:32,220
Of course. Our image has taken a hit.

359
00:23:32,340 --> 00:23:35,780
Apparently headquarters is
thinking of demoting you five ranks.

360
00:23:35,880 --> 00:23:36,200
No way!

361
00:23:36,700 --> 00:23:39,420
And from today, that's your desk.

362
00:23:43,260 --> 00:23:45,900
Because of you, headquarters cut our budget.

363
00:23:45,900 --> 00:23:48,020
Use that desk for about two years.

364
00:23:49,920 --> 00:23:50,800
It's chilly, isn't it.

365
00:23:51,220 --> 00:23:54,300
I'm frail, so I might catch a cold.

366
00:23:54,960 --> 00:23:57,180
No, you definitely won't catch a cold.

367
00:23:57,180 --> 00:23:59,840
You have the world's strongest antibodies,
remember?

368
00:24:15,340 --> 00:24:25,320
Surprise and commotion, at the right moment,
a swift solution, an unerring prediction

369
00:24:26,480 --> 00:24:35,280
Decided, a flash of inspiration, bouncing along,
gathered together, action, soaring away

370
00:24:36,200 --> 00:24:39,520
Above all, sumo power

371
00:24:39,520 --> 00:24:46,020
Gather everyone, come here

372
00:24:46,720 --> 00:24:52,240
Like a dream, the final energy

373
00:24:53,320 --> 00:24:56,720
Gazing at tomorrow, believing in yesterday

374
00:24:56,720 --> 00:24:59,620
Painting the universe,
standing on the ground

375
00:24:59,620 --> 00:25:03,420
Kameari's star spun around in a circle

376
00:25:05,520 --> 00:25:07,060
This should be good enough, right?

377
00:25:07,060 --> 00:25:08,540
Of course it's not good enough, you idiot!

378
00:25:21,020 --> 00:25:21,920
Senpai

379
00:25:21,920 --> 00:25:23,040
What's wrong, Honda?

380
00:25:23,040 --> 00:25:27,300
It's that my dad and my little brother had a huge fight
over whether or not to take over the family business.

381
00:25:27,300 --> 00:25:28,420
You should take it over.

382
00:25:28,420 --> 00:25:30,740
Yes, you're right, but that's not it.

383
00:25:30,740 --> 00:25:31,760
What's different?

384
00:25:31,760 --> 00:25:34,060
My family is a little unusual.

385
00:25:34,060 --> 00:25:36,320
Next time: The Honda family clan

386
00:25:36,320 --> 00:25:37,380
Look forward to it.

387
00:25:42,260 --> 00:25:43,660
Thank you for watching.

